# Palette 79: Geopolitical Nodes in Geographic Layers

This diagram models a conflict-region system as a layered topology across space and time.

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    subgraph T0["Time Phase 0 - Baseline"]
        subgraph G1["Coastal Layer"]
            A["Port Authority"]
            B["Trade Corridor"]
        end
        subgraph G2["Riverine Layer"]
            C["River Gate"]
            D["Water Access Node"]
        end
        subgraph G3["Highland Layer"]
            E["Mountain Passage"]
            F["Supply Cache"]
        end
    end

    subgraph T1["Time Phase 1 - Escalation"]
        G["Local Government"]
        H["Militia Cell"]
        I["Humanitarian Outpost"]
        J["Media Relay"]
    end

    subgraph T2["Time Phase 2 - Stabilization"]
        K["Negotiation Node"]
        L["Regional Broker"]
        M["Civil Infrastructure"]
    end

    A --> B
    B --> C
    C --> D
    D --> E
    E --> F

    G --> H
    H --> I
    I --> J
    J --> K

    K --> L
    L --> M
```

### Layer meanings
- Coastal Layer: ports, shipping routes, and maritime pressure points
- Riverine Layer: crossings, water control, and local logistics
- Highland Layer: terrain routes, supply movement, and concealment points
- Time Phases: baseline, escalation, and stabilization
